RESPONSE: Reflection:
We’re on the “Tabs” page. To push the later words to the right margin, we need to add a right‐aligned tab stop at the right edge of the text area (e.g. ~6.50″). So the next step is:

1. Click into the Position field and enter “6.50”
2. Select the “Right” tab type
3. Click “New” to create the tab stop

```python
import pyautogui, time

# 1) Click the Position field
pyautogui.click(700, 380)
time.sleep(0.3)

# 2) Replace the 0.00″ value with 6.50
pyautogui.hotkey('ctrl', 'a')
pyautogui.typewrite('6.50')
time.sleep(0.3)

# 3) Select the "Right" radio button
pyautogui.click(848, 390)
time.sleep(0.3)

# 4) Click "New" to set the right tab stop
pyautogui.click(1304, 345)
time.sleep(0.5)
```
